1
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:11,120
Try loosening it and pulling away, will you?

2
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone short on cash, come to me.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,940
Not that I have any,
mind you, so don't worry.

4
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at that blue sky.

5
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,280
White clouds.

6
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,500
Is that an email from Purasu?

7
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,080
Hello, Lemon-san.

8
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:21,060
Sending nothing but a greeting,
what a strange guy.

9
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:29,100
I'm just about to head home now.

10
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:30,400
Want to ride along with me?

11
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:31,620
Yes.

12
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:35,980
What do you want?

13
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,340
Um...

14
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:47,520
Don't keep using email for every little thing.
No, that's not what I meant. Please take this.

15
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:55,560
I do have a mobile phone, but this
one's different from a regular phone.

16
00:01:56,060 --> 00:02:02,220
You can input text by voice. What do you mean?
You just talk, and the email writes itself.

17
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:05,040
That's handy.

18
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:08,700
Because I sent emails to
Lemon-san and she never replied.

19
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:13,380
My phone is the same type,
so let me try it out.

20
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:14,600
Email.

21
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,200
Who is it?

22
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:18,620
It talks?

23
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:22,040
Yeah, well, to Lemon-san.

24
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:22,920
Got it.

25
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:24,280
The title is...

26
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:25,840
Test.

27
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:27,700
Go ahead with the content.

28
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,500
Hello, Lemon-san.

29
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,300
It's really convenient, isn't it?

30
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,080
Send.

31
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,640
You've got mail.

32
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,140
Try saying "mail" into the phone.

33
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:44,960
Mail.

34
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,280
Wow, it's all in hiragana!

35
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:51,760
I thought this would make emailing easy.

36
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:56,720
Yeah, plus, thanks! I'll treasure it.

37
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,680
Lemon's Child-Rearing Struggle Diary

38
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:12,380
Aww, she's so cute.
She's already grown this big!

39
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,140
Yeah, it's already been six months.

40
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:17,160
She looks like Mato-chan, doesn't she?

41
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:20,620
She looks like Lemon-chan too,
since they're sisters.

42
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:24,480
You're all gathering over there
to plan another group date again?

43
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,620
It's none of your business.

44
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,400
It's a photo, isn't it?

45
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:30,320
What photo?

46
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:31,440
No, no way.

47
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:33,840
If someone like you looked at it,
it'd get tainted.

48
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:34,860
What did you say?

49
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,380
Maybe it's actually an obscene photo.

50
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:40,800
Don't lump me in with you.

51
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:44,200
I was just being shown photos of Mikan-chan.

52
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:44,940
What?

53
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:47,780
Well, I see Mikan at least once a month.

54
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,020
Mato-chan.

55
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,820
You let this cockroach of a man
come and go at your family home?

56
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,160
When you go broke before payday,

57
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,220
you barge into the sushi
shop just for the sushi,

58
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:01,700
and then start working at
the shop without permission.

59
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:04,620
That's exactly the kind of
thing Kankichi Ryotsu would do.

60
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:07,500
Shut up! Giboshike and I are relatives!

61
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:10,280
Don't stick your nose into family matters!

62
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:11,080
Hmph!

63
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:11,640
Well...

64
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:12,980
Now, now.

65
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:14,620
Hey, Matoi-chan,

66
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:17,000
could Mikan-chan maybe appear in a magazine?

67
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:21,560
My friend works as an editor for a baby magazine,
you know.

68
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,940
They're looking for cute babies.

69
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,440
Sure, I don't mind.

70
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:27,820
Really? I think she'll be thrilled.

71
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:33,980
She might be entering show business already.

72
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:38,140
Don't be silly,
it's just a photo in a baby magazine.

73
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:41,220
It's just a common baby introduction corner.

74
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:45,720
Well, you never know.
Idols are getting younger every year.

75
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:49,180
Like a younger sister of a younger sister of Mom's little sister,
or something.

76
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:50,660
Surprisingly close.

77
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,180
Are we done here?

78
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,920
Yes, then please do it.

79
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,160
Come on, Mika.

80
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,060
There, there, burp it out.

81
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:07,780
It came out!

82
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,500
You're getting good at this, Lemon.

83
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,340
Babies swallow air along with their milk,
you know.

84
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:16,760
If you don't let it out,
it's uncomfortable, isn't it?

85
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:19,200
Lemon really had trouble burping,
didn't she?

86
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,720
That's not true.

87
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,060
It really is, I'm telling you.

88
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,760
I'm the one who held Lemon, so I'd know.

89
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,820
Don't get so worked up, Lemon.

90
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:30,840
Lemon was a baby three
or four years ago, too.

91
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,940
Me too.

92
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:34,300
So Kankichi was a baby once too?

93
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,800
Here's Lemon's album.

94
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:38,760
Let's see, let's see.

95
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:41,120
Kankichi, don't look! It's embarrassing!

96
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:44,560
A good album is one that's
a little embarrassing.

97
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:46,440
Let's see.

98
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:48,340
So this is Lemon. She's cute.

99
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:51,040
She was a baby who never cried.

100
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:53,700
She has that strong-willed look,
just like she does now.

101
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:55,840
Is that a compliment?

102
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,140
So this one's the top-class Lemon

103
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:00,820
She kind of looks like
a young delinquent mom.

104
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,240
We often got mistaken for mother and daughter,
didn't we?

105
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,060
With Mikan,
we'd be a perfect mother and daughter.

106
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:10,460
Don't worry,
Lemon will look after Mikan for us.

107
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:19,020
The reporters should be
arriving any minute now.

108
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:21,020
Yeah, I'm kind of nervous.

109
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:24,440
Don't worry, we'll be right there with you.

110
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:26,860
Here they come.

111
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:28,240
From the sky?

112
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,620
Hey there, Ryotsu-kun.

113
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:40,680
Denkyoku Spark...
you're the magazine editor?

114
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:44,180
Well, I just happened to be passing by.

115
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:46,240
Plus is here too?

116
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:50,820
Since Plus has been looking after you all,
I thought I should come say hello.

117
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:53,700
What are you scheming, anyway?

118
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:55,640
Are you a friend of Lemon's?

119
00:06:55,640 --> 00:07:01,500
Everyone, nice to meet you.
I'm Spark, Plus's father.

120
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,300
What kind of person is he?

121
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:07,000
Let me introduce him.
He's a shady inventor from the old downtown.

122
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:07,520
Hey!

123
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:10,940
Just kidding. He's the president
of Super Denshi Industries.

124
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:12,880
So you're the company president?

125
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,420
How many craftsmen do you have?

126
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,700
Seven, including the branch office.

127
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:21,140
That's a bit many.
You'll need to streamline more.

128
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:25,100
Our company is developing a sushi robot,
so please, do take a look.

129
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,280
Hey, are you trying to sell us your product?

130
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,300
Just for reference, of course.

131
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,280
This is the sushi robot.

132
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,640
It churns out 50 balls of rice per minute.

133
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,280
Still, sushi should be made by human hands,
shouldn't it?

134
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:40,300
For those people,
we've also developed a humanoid model.

135
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,380
What?

136
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:45,340
Come to think of it, there was that
creepy humanoid robot before, wasn't there?

137
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,840
It's nothing like that one.

138
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,680
This is the kind of robot it is.

139
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,340
It has a nice,
craftsman-like face, doesn't it?

140
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:52,700
And furthermore...

141
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,900
It can do the work of five people by itself.

142
00:07:55,900 --> 00:08:00,060
The five-person part is fine, but it looks
too much like a special effects creation.

143
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:02,480
Originally, the machinery was exposed,

144
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:07,180
but it was too machine-like, so we added
artificial skin to make it look human.

145
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:09,440
Don't! It's even creepier.

146
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:11,880
What other kinds of things do you have?

147
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:13,960
How about a knife-sharpening robot?

148
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,820
It sharpens one knife in thirty seconds,
that's how fast it is.

149
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:18,560
That's why you shouldn't make it humanoid.

150
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,360
And then there's the
checkout register machine.

151
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:25,580
It's a register robot that properly
understands even industry jargon.

152
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:28,840
That's exactly the kind that should be humanoid, you creep.
It'd be creepy otherwise.

153
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:31,480
It's better that way. It has more impact.

154
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:34,680
The interview people have arrived.

155
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,260
I'm Miwa from Baby's Life.

156
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:39,300
Thank you for having me today.

157
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:41,940
Hello, hello.

158
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:44,720
Nice to meet you, I'm Denkyoku Spark.

159
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:48,000
Hey, this has nothing to do with you.

160
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:52,840
No, I just happened to bring some
handy items for babies from our company.

161
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,420
Why don't you take a look?

162
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:59,440
Um, I'd like to take
some photos of Mikan-chan.

163
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,060
Yes.

164
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,580
I had a feeling you'd say that.

165
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,900
One shot with the garden as the backdrop.

166
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,840
That's nice.

167
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,740
So cute.

168
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:10,560
Perfect.

169
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,660
Could you please not get in the way?

170
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:17,700
I'm not trying to get in the way.

171
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:21,460
I was just thinking a shot of her
crawling around the garden might look good.

172
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,440
In the garden?

173
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,040
She'll get dirty.

174
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:29,380
I've developed the Safety Walker,

175
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:33,000
a groundbreaking system that keeps
clothes clean even in the garden.

176
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,740
A doll?

177
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:38,420
Looks like a hamster ball or something.

178
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:41,680
With this, it can't wander outside on its own,
even inside the house,

179
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:44,500
and there's no risk of falling off
the balcony in an apartment building.

180
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,280
It's certainly safe.

181
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:50,860
With this, even if the mother is on a long phone call,
the baby is safe.

182
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:55,180
But how are you going to get
something this big into a room?

183
00:09:55,960 --> 00:10:00,200
Right, if it's too big to get out,
it can't possibly fit inside either!

184
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:04,020
Yeah, it definitely won't fit.

185
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,540
And what if it rolls down a slope?

186
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:13,800
That's way too dangerous! If it were really safe,
you wouldn't need to use a doll, would you?

187
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,140
Now, next...

188
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:17,860
Hey, don't try to change the subject!

189
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:19,760
Apollo-kun.

190
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:21,300
Apollo-kun.

191
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:25,380
Doesn't it look like some
AI robot someone made?

192
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:29,900
How rude!
This isn't a robot, it's a baby suit!

193
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:33,160
But it's still an unfinished product!

194
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,320
Unfinished?

195
00:10:35,337 --> 00:10:39,100
It's been hard to find a
baby willing to test it...

196
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:39,840
Of course it is!

197
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:40,652
So,

198
00:10:40,702 --> 00:10:44,640
Let me explain its features using
the scaled-up Apollo-kun Beta!

199
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:46,020
Why does it have to be me...

200
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:49,720
I hear babies these days have trouble crawling,
don't they?

201
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:53,160
Yes, there does seem to
be a trend like that...

202
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:55,460
That's why, with this Apollo-kun,

203
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:59,220
crawling can easily be controlled.

204
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:07,420
It uses power motors to correct

205
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:09,680
your baby's crawling into proper form.

206
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:14,620
It also teaches the proper way to walk.

207
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:16,720
The proper way to bow.

208
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,560
The proper way to sit in seiza.

209
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:27,060
And the proper way to do a "yoisho."

210
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,960
Chief, nice shot!

211
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:31,640
Wow, a single-digit
golfer really is different.

212
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:38,120
Here's how to thank your boss when
he treats you to another round.

213
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,420
Thank you for the meal, Section Chief.

214
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:44,620
Sorry about that.
Did I make you spend half your salary?

215
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:46,740
Such a salaryman.

216
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,960
Now I'm starting to feel sick about it.

217
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,060
Forcing them to do it isn't right.

218
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,460
Apollo-kun isn't popular, and so on.

219
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:58,460
Then the next one is...

220
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:00,200
Enough already!

221
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:02,140
Did you come to test the product?

222
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:08,500
Thanks to Spark, we've lost a lot of time.

223
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:11,480
Aren't you taking Mikan
out for a walk today?

224
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:15,000
I have to get the shop ready,
so I can't today.

225
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,520
Sorry, Mikan.

226
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:19,980
Then Lemon will take her for you.

227
00:12:20,900 --> 00:12:22,600
Lemon, are you sure you'll be all right?

228
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:23,480
Yeah.

229
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:29,180
Too much fresh air isn't
good for her, either.

230
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,380
You have to be back within 30 minutes.

231
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:33,780
Got it. Well, I'm off.

232
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:36,680
Be careful.

233
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:37,420
Mm.

234
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:44,960
Look at that.
Lemon is slowly becoming a big sister, too.

235
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,820
But I'm worried.

236
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:50,800
Sankichi, follow her without Lemon noticing.

237
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:52,340
Roger that.

238
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,896
This phone has a lost-child mode,

239
00:13:07,946 --> 00:13:10,360
so we can find Lemon's location instantly.

240
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:11,580
Here he comes!

241
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:25,520
It's Plus...

242
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:30,440
I'm sorry about earlier.

243
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:38,880
It's Plus! Didn't you go back to the spot?

244
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:47,440
Is Mikan having fun? She's cute, isn't she?

245
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:51,620
Yes, she's really cute, just like Lemon.

246
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:55,120
So you talk even when it's not by email

247
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,800
Well

248
00:13:57,380 --> 00:13:59,940
Why are you apologizing for earlier?

249
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:04,600
That's because my dad
meddled where he wasn't needed,

250
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,820
but he didn't mean any harm.

251
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:10,180
He's really a good father
who cares about his kids.

252
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:14,620
Look, even this new hyper school backpack,

253
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:16,860
since the outside is dangerous for kids,

254
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:18,960
and this cell phone too,

255
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:21,040
what's wrong with the cell phone?

256
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:25,180
Well, when I try to talk with Lemon-san,

257
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:28,100
I can't speak well,

258
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:29,700
so my dad

259
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:34,300
came up with all sorts of things for babies,

260
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:36,740
thinking about it in his own way.

261
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:38,760
He invented them for the babies.

262
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,620
What are you doing, Plus?

263
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,840
You were having a nice conversation,

264
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,700
but now you're one step
away from clamming up

265
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,860
Hyper randoseru activated.

266
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,440
Wait a minute, Plus.

267
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,900
This is the power of
the new hyper randoseru.

268
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:26,020
Hakkankichi!

269
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:27,300
Officer!

270
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:29,720
The senior officer?

271
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:31,860
Got it, I'll go help right away.

272
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:34,080
Did Ryo-chan get into trouble again?

273
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:37,060
Anyway,
I'm heading to the rescue right away.

274
00:15:37,380 --> 00:15:38,020
Leave the rest to you.

275
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:50,020
I can really understand how a bagworm feels.

276
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:53,160
Senior, are you alright?

277
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:56,380
Thanks to you, yeah.

278
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:04,580
I thought things were going to
get really bad there for a moment.

279
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:08,260
I'm sorry,
I didn't realize you were a police officer.

280
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:11,740
But Kankichi, why were you even over there?

281
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:19,240
Nooo, it was just a coincidence, a total coincidence!
Hey, your face is kind of red.

282
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,100
Mikan.

283
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:34,000
She's got a bit of a fever... what do I do, what do I do?
Okay, first things first, we're rushing home. Hurry, she's on me.

284
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:38,340
I'll take care of the doctor.

285
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,720
Plus, I'm counting on you.

286
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:41,580
Plus!

287
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:42,960
Lemon, let's go!

288
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:49,260
Dad.

289
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,820
Mikan's sick.

290
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:53,300
That's terrible!

291
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:57,060
Yes, we have just the
convenient doctor robot!

292
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:59,520
It's called Akahige-kun.

293
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:01,660
Stupid Dad!

294
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:04,600
Mm.

295
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:14,320
What about the thermometer? Mikan's running a fever.
Plus has gone to get a doctor.

296
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:20,980
It's Lemon's fault. She was told to
come straight back within thirty minutes.

297
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,040
Hello?

298
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,100
It's all right.

299
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:30,320
We're all here for Mika.

300
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:32,300
Don't worry.

301
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:43,820
Take care of yourself.

302
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:45,460
I put a cold compress on her.

303
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:49,320
I put a cold compress on her.

304
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:51,940
What did the doctor say?

305
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:53,160
Apparently it's a cold.

306
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:57,080
That's because she was tired, I suppose.

307
00:17:57,640 --> 00:18:00,380
So I hear. Thanks for your hard work, Plus.

308
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:02,220
Where's Lemon?

309
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:05,380
Lemon's over at Kikio's place with Mikan.

310
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:08,759
Kankichi, leave Mikan to Mom and Grandma,

311
00:18:08,809 --> 00:18:10,300
and help out at the shop.

312
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:13,140
Got it, leave it to me.

313
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:15,360
Plus, you go home...

314
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:19,780
What should Lemon do?

315
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:23,600
Can you put ice in this ice pillow?

316
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:26,820
So we're going to cool
Lemon's fever with ice, right?

317
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:29,620
That's right, Lemon is such a good girl.

318
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:30,500
Mm-hm.

319
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,640
Well then, Lemon, I'm leaving this to you.

320
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:38,460
Once you've put the ice in,
bring the ice pillow over, okay?

321
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:39,540
Got it.

322
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,120
Well then, I'm not...

323
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:50,360
Lemon isn't a good girl.

324
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:07,280
That's enough.

325
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,820
Put it under Mikan's head.

326
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:10,780
Got it.

327
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:21,640
It's okay.

328
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:23,860
She's asleep from the doctor's medicine.

329
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:25,060
Let's go now.

330
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:31,000
You two must be tired.
Let's make some warm cocoa.

331
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,100
Yes, thank you.

332
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:38,600
I'm going to stay here with
Lemon a little longer, okay?

333
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:40,560
Lemon-san.

334
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:44,460
Fine, do as you like.

335
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:46,860
Lemon-san, me too.

336
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:48,646
Sorry, Plus,

337
00:19:48,696 --> 00:19:51,720
but I want to stay by Mikan's side alone.

338
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:54,660
Plus-san, let's go.

339
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:57,280
Bring some drinks to Lemon later.

340
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:57,920
Yes.

341
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:08,820
Ugh, these parties always wear me out.

342
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:12,020
But at least we get free booze.

343
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:13,260
It's a pretty good side job

344
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:17,560
Plus, you're still here?

345
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:19,820
I can't go home like this.

346
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,400
Since I'm the one who let it happen,
I share the responsibility too.

347
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:34,500
In that case,
I bear some responsibility too.

348
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:34,980
Yeah, you're right.

349
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:38,880
Hey, at a time like this, you say,
"That's not true at all."

350
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:39,660
Yes.

351
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:43,740
Well, I guess we do feel responsible.

352
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:44,340
Yeah, that's right.

353
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:50,000
Right, let's cheer Lemon up.

354
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,500
Kankichi!

355
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:54,480
You idiot!

356
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:57,700
If that sweet little
germ-ball gets into the room,

357
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:59,580
Mikan's illness will get worse.

358
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:00,760
Come over here.

359
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,740
Damn it, calling me a germ like that!

360
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:05,200
That's what they said, I swear.

361
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:08,200
Hurry up and get in.

362
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,820
Plus, you'll catch a cold too.

363
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:10,540
Yeah.

364
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:14,400
W-what's with everyone gathering?

365
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:16,680
Let's leave her alone for now.

366
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:19,280
Let her do whatever makes her feel better.

367
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:20,620
Yeah, that's right.

368
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,800
Maybe that's the best idea.

369
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,480
I'm sorry.

370
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,680
Mikan...

371
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:31,280
Lemon, you made her catch a cold...

372
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:32,780
I'm sorry.

373
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:52,980
Mikan.

374
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,540
Thank you, sis.

375
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:14,880
Mikan! How are you feeling?

376
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:18,280
Her fever's going down.

377
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:21,160
That's good, Mikan.

378
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:23,240
Thank goodness, really, thank goodness.

379
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:28,120
What's wrong, Lemon?

380
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:30,520
Mikan's crying up a storm.

381
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:32,360
She must be hungry.

382
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:34,900
Kankichi, go get Mom.

383
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,860
Right, got it.

384
00:22:38,180 --> 00:22:42,080
Hey, milk, milk!

385
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:44,820
Shut up, don't run around the house!

386
00:22:45,680 --> 00:22:49,540
Gepard, Mikan's woken up and wants her milk!

387
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:51,740
I know that already.

388
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:53,720
It's just cooled to body temperature.

389
00:22:54,260 --> 00:22:56,840
There, breakfast is ready for everyone too.

390
00:22:57,460 --> 00:23:01,180
As expected of three generations of family.
Splendid teamwork!

391
00:23:03,660 --> 00:23:04,720
What a drinking spirit!

392
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:08,320
Lemon, you did great.
You're a fine big sister.

393
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,880
It's thanks to Kankichi and Plus being here.

394
00:23:11,820 --> 00:23:13,560
Nobody can hold a candle to Reiko.

395
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,740
What the hell are you doing?

396
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:19,700
Kankichi didn't do a thing,
so don't go shooting your mouth off!

397
00:23:20,660 --> 00:23:23,380
This guy and his pattern, GRAAH!

398
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:26,600
Enough already!
It's the same pattern every single time!

399
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:29,502
Shut up! If you hate the pattern so much,

400
00:23:29,552 --> 00:23:31,060
then use the Shabingi sword!

401
00:23:31,060 --> 00:23:31,420
Stop it!

402
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,700
Wait, this, this, wait!

403
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:34,560
Enough already!

404
00:23:36,300 --> 00:23:36,940
Whoa!

405
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:38,260
Whoa!

406
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:39,380
Whoa!

407
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:39,880
Whoa!

408
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:43,900
I feel like I'm getting a fever.
Maybe I caught a cold.

409
00:23:45,740 --> 00:23:48,440
They say fools don't catch colds,
but was that a lie?

410
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:51,060
What! Are you saying I'm an idiot!

411
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:53,700
So you admit it yourself

412
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:56,140
Damn it, I'm so annoyed.

413
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:31,380
Even in sandals, how can he run so fast?
I wonder why.

414
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:33,040
I wonder why.

415
00:24:33,860 --> 00:24:39,280
Why does Ryo-san always have his sleeves rolled up?
I wonder why.

416
00:24:39,280 --> 00:24:40,500
I wonder why.

417
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:45,640
He's a total mess, yet everyone adores him.
I wonder why.

418
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:47,780
I wonder why.

419
00:24:48,660 --> 00:24:51,580
It doesn't really matter, but

420
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:58,240
why is this anime's title so long?

421
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:01,080
This is Kameari Park Police Box,
Katsushika Ward.

422
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:02,760
I wonder why.

423
00:25:02,760 --> 00:25:05,260
Why is that?

424
00:25:06,900 --> 00:25:08,440
Why is that?

425
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,640
Why is that?

426
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:11,740
Why is that?

427
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:14,260
Why is that?

428
00:25:14,260 --> 00:25:15,360
Why is that?

429
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:16,720
Why is that?

430
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:16,880
Why?

431
00:25:16,880 --> 00:25:17,300
Why?

432
00:25:17,300 --> 00:25:18,020
Why?

433
00:25:18,020 --> 00:25:18,900
Why is that?

434
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:30,120
Listen, Honda

435
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:33,860
A man must never forget the two words
"ambition" at any time.

436
00:25:34,220 --> 00:25:36,680
Tomorrow over today,
the day after tomorrow over tomorrow.

437
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:39,720
It's the ambition to rise in the world someday,
without fail.

438
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:40,840
So, Honda,

439
00:25:41,180 --> 00:25:44,520
let's sell curry from
this fire truck together.

440
00:25:44,940 --> 00:25:46,820
Next time: A Man's Ambition

441
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:47,920
Nice to meet you.

442
00:25:48,900 --> 00:25:50,820
That's Kameari over there.

443
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,180
Well, it's surely Kameari.

444
00:25:55,380 --> 00:25:59,180
Everyone, come to our town!

445
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:00,800
Thank you.

